## Why This Is Asked
Examines practical isolation controls for logs in multi-tenant cloud-native systems, including data-minimization, policy enforcement, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped logging
- ABAC/OPA policy enforcement at ingestion
- Data redaction and least-privilege exporters
- SPIRE/mTLS between log agents and collectors
- Ephemeral credentials rotation and secrets hygiene

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactForTenant(log, tenantId) {
  const redacted = {...log};
  const sensitiveKeys = ['ssn','creditCard','dob','email'];
  for (const k of sensitiveKeys) {
    if (redacted[k] && redacted.tenantId === tenantId) {
      redacted[k] = '[REDACTED]';
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for cross-tenant access in search results?
- What monitoring signals indicate redaction failures or policy drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical application of phishing-resistant MFA and device-based access in admin contexts, plus rollout, exceptions, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn)
- passwordless SSO
- device posture (MDM/EMM)
- conditional access rules
- centralized logging (SIEM) and phishing simulations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example simple authorization gate
function allowAccess(user, device) {
  const okUser = user.isAdmin;
  const okDevice = device.isCompliant;
  const okMFA = user.mfaCompletedWithFido2;
  return okUser && okDevice && okMFA;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a lost FIDO key or key compromise?
- What metrics would you track to gauge phishing-resistant MFA effectiveness?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end security of hybrid AI platforms, spanning software supply chain and model governance, with practical incident response capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Secure software supply chain and model governance
- SBOMs, image/model signing, and cryptographic attestations
- Provenance verification and reproducible builds
- Policy-as-Code enforcement with OPA Gatekeeper
- Runtime attestation in Kubernetes environments
- Data provenance tracking for training datasets
- Incident response playbooks and success metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: sign an image with cosign
const { execSync } = require('child_process');

function signContainerImage(imageUrl) {
  // Generate SBOM
  execSync(`syft ${imageUrl} -o cyclonedx-json > sbom.json`);

  // Sign the image
  execSync(`cosign sign --key cosign.key ${imageUrl}`);

  // Attach SBOM as attestation
  execSync(`cosign attest --predicate sbom.json --type cyclonedx ${imageUrl}`);

  console.log(`Successfully signed ${imageUrl}`);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to apply fundamental security controls to third-party components—a common real-world risk at many companies. It evaluates your understanding of vendor vetting, data minimization, privacy controls, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Third-party risk management
- Data minimization and PII redaction
- User consent and privacy controls
- Observability and incident response readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: redact PII from analytics payload
function redact(payload) {
  const redacted = { ...payload };
  if (redacted.userEmail) redacted.userEmail = "[REDACTED]";
  if (redacted.userPhone) redacted.userPhone = "[REDACTED]";
  return redacted;
}

// Example: hash identifiers before transmission
function hashIdentifier(identifier) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(identifier).digest('hex');
}
```
